A||||3||Double07||Clicking noise||||1||
Z||000000||Double07||09-22-2000||01:49 PM||||My 86 fiero, 4 speed, v6 has a clicking noise from the engine, could it be a lifter? what can be done to fix it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||LAMBO||09-22-2000||02:41 PM||||Yes, it could be a lifter. Or it could be an exhaust leak (its amazing how much an exhaust leak will sound like a stuck lifter) or it could be just the normal clicking from your fuel injection. Sometimes, a little oil additive like JB or Berrymans will unstick lifters, but usually, especially if you've got quite a few miles on the car, new lifters are in order. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Check carefully for exhaust leaks first, especially around the exhaust manifolds. The welds are prone to breaking loose, or bolts breaking off. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Finally, if your exhaust is really quiet, and the ticking noise is subtle, then its probably just your injectors, no worry! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||the need for speed||09-22-2000||06:54 PM||||I have an 87 gt v6, I have noticed a clicking noise from the engine when I turn on the defrost or the vents for heat or cold air, but not if I turn on the heater. I have looked in the engine and it seems that it is the air conditioner, the end will spin every 10 to 15 seconds. It is loud when sitting still, does any one know why it is doing this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||EdsB52||09-22-2000||07:01 PM||||The a/c cycles every 10-15 seconds because it is out or very low on freon. Why it makes noise while the compressor is not operating, I don't know. If the noise is definately comming from the compressor clutch assy, it could be the bearing in the clutch. Either way, don't cycle the compressor until you add a little oil and / or service it with freon. You may not have smoked it yet!||||reg||1
